  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $T(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k$\n- $U(t)=2t\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j-\\sqrt{t}\\,k$\n- $V(x,y,z)={e}^{-2z}\\sqrt{x+y}$",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $T(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $U(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
